X squared minus 2 X plus 1 has generation sizes satisfying the Table 5 recurrence with coefficients 3, -3, 1 at every index at least 3.\n+\n+**Definition 1.1 (The double-root polynomial).**\n+\n+$$(\\operatorname{q}: \\operatorname{Polynomial}\\left(\\mathbb{Z}\\right)) = \\operatorname{Polynomial.X}^{2} - 2 \\cdot \\operatorname{Polynomial.X} + 1$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.q` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Christian Ballot, Clark Kimberling and Peter J. C. Moses (2017). *Linear Recurrences Originating From Polynomial Trees*. DOI: [10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731](https://doi.org/10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731). URL: <https://www.fq.math.ca/Papers1/55-5/BallotKimberlingMoses.pdf>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Table 5, p. 23, gives the row q(x) = x² − 2x + 1, Gₙ = 1,1,2,4,7,11,16,22,29,37,46, and linear recurrence 3,−3,1. Here X is Polynomial.X over the integers.\n+\n+**Definition 1.2 (The addition child).**\n+\n+$$\\forall (p: \\operatorname{Polynomial}\\left(\\mathbb{Z}\\right)), (\\operatorname{addChild}\\left(p\\right) = \\operatorname{Polynomial.modByMonic}\\left(p + 1, \\operatorname{q}\\right))$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.addChild` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Christian Ballot, Clark Kimberling and Peter J. C. Moses (2017). *Linear Recurrences Originating From Polynomial Trees*. DOI: [10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731](https://doi.org/10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731). URL: <https://www.fq.math.ca/Papers1/55-5/BallotKimberlingMoses.pdf>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Section 1, p. 15: “Let T∗ be the set of polynomials in x generated by these rules: 0 ∈ T∗, and if p ∈ T∗, then p + 1 ∈ T∗ and xp ∈ T∗.” Section 1, p. 17: “Then the substitution of qₘ₋₁xᵐ⁻¹ + ⋯ + q₁x + q₀ for xᵐ throughout T∗ produces a labeling of T∗ that includes duplicates.” “For the top-to-bottom order, we denote the resulting tree by T(q(x)).” “Note that T(q(x)) can be regarded as T∗ mod q(x).” The addition child is the monic remainder of p + 1 modulo q in Polynomial ℤ.\n+\n+**Definition 1.3 (The multiplication child).**\n+\n+$$\\forall (p: \\operatorname{Polynomial}\\left(\\mathbb{Z}\\right)), (\\operatorname{mulChild}\\left(p\\right) = \\operatorname{Polynomial.modByMonic}\\left(\\operatorname{Polynomial.X} \\cdot p, \\operatorname{q}\\right))$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.mulChild` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Christian Ballot, Clark Kimberling and Peter J. C. Moses (2017). *Linear Recurrences Originating From Polynomial Trees*. DOI: [10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731](https://doi.org/10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731). URL: <https://www.fq.math.ca/Papers1/55-5/BallotKimberlingMoses.pdf>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Section 1, p. 15: “Let T∗ be the set of polynomials in x generated by these rules: 0 ∈ T∗, and if p ∈ T∗, then p + 1 ∈ T∗ and xp ∈ T∗.” Section 1, p. 17: “Then the substitution of qₘ₋₁xᵐ⁻¹ + ⋯ + q₁x + q₀ for xᵐ throughout T∗ produces a labeling of T∗ that includes duplicates.” “For the top-to-bottom order, we denote the resulting tree by T(q(x)).” “Note that T(q(x)) can be regarded as T∗ mod q(x).” The multiplication child is the monic remainder of X * p modulo q in Polynomial ℤ.\n+\n+**Definition 1.4 (All labels reached within a given depth).**\n+\n+$$(\\operatorname{seen}\\left(0\\right) = \\operatorname{Finset.singleton}\\left((0: \\operatorname{Polynomial}\\left(\\mathbb{Z}\\right))\\right)) \\land (\\forall (n: \\mathbb{N}), (\\operatorname{seen}\\left(n + 1\\right) = \\operatorname{Finset.union}\\left(\\operatorname{Finset.union}\\left(\\operatorname{seen}\\left(n\\right), \\operatorname{Finset.image}\\left(\\operatorname{addChild}, \\operatorname{seen}\\left(n\\right)\\right)\\right), \\operatorname{Finset.image}\\left(\\operatorname{mulChild}, \\operatorname{seen}\\left(n\\right)\\right)\\right)))$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.seen` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Christian Ballot, Clark Kimberling and Peter J. C. Moses (2017). *Linear Recurrences Originating From Polynomial Trees*. DOI: [10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731](https://doi.org/10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731). URL: <https://www.fq.math.ca/Papers1/55-5/BallotKimberlingMoses.pdf>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Section 1, p. 15: “Let T∗ be the set of polynomials in x generated by these rules: 0 ∈ T∗, and if p ∈ T∗, then p + 1 ∈ T∗ and xp ∈ T∗.” Section 1, p. 17: “Then the substitution of qₘ₋₁xᵐ⁻¹ + ⋯ + q₁x + q₀ for xᵐ throughout T∗ produces a labeling of T∗ that includes duplicates.” “For the top-to-bottom order, we denote the resulting tree by T(q(x)).” “Note that T(q(x)) can be regarded as T∗ mod q(x).” The finite set seen n contains every distinct label reached in at most n operations, including the zero root. It accumulates the old labels and both child images, so multiplicities and the choice of a parent among equal labels have no effect.\n+\n+**Definition 1.5 (The generation sets).**\n+\n+$$(\\operatorname{generation}\\left(0\\right) = \\operatorname{Finset.singleton}\\left((0: \\operatorname{Polynomial}\\left(\\mathbb{Z}\\right))\\right)) \\land (\\forall (n: \\mathbb{N}), (\\operatorname{generation}\\left(n + 1\\right) = \\operatorname{seen}\\left(n + 1\\right) \\setminus \\operatorname{seen}\\left(n\\right)))$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.generation` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Christian Ballot, Clark Kimberling and Peter J. C. Moses (2017). *Linear Recurrences Originating From Polynomial Trees*. DOI: [10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731](https://doi.org/10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731). URL: <https://www.fq.math.ca/Papers1/55-5/BallotKimberlingMoses.pdf>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Section 1, p. 15: “We regard T∗ as a tree that grows in successive generations: g(0) = {0}, g(1) = {1}, g(2) = {2,x}, g(3) = {3,2x,x + 1,x²} g(4) = {4,3x,2x + 1,2x²,x + 2,x² + x,x² + 1,x³}, and so on, as in Figure 1.” Section 1, p. 17: “Then the substitution of qₘ₋₁xᵐ⁻¹ + ⋯ + q₁x + q₀ for xᵐ throughout T∗ produces a labeling of T∗ that includes duplicates.” “For the top-to-bottom order, we denote the resulting tree by T(q(x)).” “Note that T(q(x)) can be regarded as T∗ mod q(x).” Generation zero is the zero root. At depth n + 1, set difference removes every label seen at an earlier depth. Finset membership counts a same-generation duplicate once. These are polynomial remainders, without evaluating X at 1.\n+\n+**Definition 1.6 (Generation cardinality).**\n+\n+$$\\forall (n: \\mathbb{N}), (\\operatorname{G}\\left(n\\right) = \\operatorname{Finset.card}\\left(\\operatorname{generation}\\left(n\\right)\\right))$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.G` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Christian Ballot, Clark Kimberling and Peter J. C. Moses (2017). *Linear Recurrences Originating From Polynomial Trees*. DOI: [10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731](https://doi.org/10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731). URL: <https://www.fq.math.ca/Papers1/55-5/BallotKimberlingMoses.pdf>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Section 1, p. 17: “Much of the paper henceforth studies the sequence (Gₙ)ₙ≥₀, where Gₙ = |g(n)| and g(n) is the nth generation of the tree T(r), for various r.” Section 5 uses these generation counts for polynomial choices q(x). Here G n is the natural-number cardinality of generation n for the selected polynomial tree.\n+\n+**Definition 1.7 (The eventual recurrence).**\n+\n+$$(\\operatorname{claim}) \\Leftrightarrow (\\exists (N: \\mathbb{N}), ((3 \\le N) \\land (\\forall (n: \\mathbb{N}), ((N \\le n) \\Rightarrow ((\\operatorname{G}\\left(n\\right): \\mathbb{Z}) = 3 \\cdot (\\operatorname{G}\\left(n - 1\\right): \\mathbb{Z}) - 3 \\cdot (\\operatorname{G}\\left(n - 2\\right): \\mathbb{Z}) + (\\operatorname{G}\\left(n - 3\\right): \\mathbb{Z}))))))$$\n+\n+*Formalization.* `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.claim` (`✓ std3`).\n+\n+*Citation.* Christian Ballot, Clark Kimberling and Peter J. C. Moses (2017). *Linear Recurrences Originating From Polynomial Trees*. DOI: [10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731](https://doi.org/10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731). URL: <https://www.fq.math.ca/Papers1/55-5/BallotKimberlingMoses.pdf>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Section 5, p. 23: “Some proofs of the computer-detected recurrences reported in Table 5 and 6 might be challenging. Most of the entries in the column headed “linear recurrence” are conjectured as “eventual”; i.e., the recurrence applies after some unspecified number of initial terms.” The selected Table 5 row is q(x) = x² − 2x + 1 with recurrence coefficients 3,−3,1. Its assertion is the existence of N ≥ 3 such that the displayed recurrence holds for every n ≥ N. All indices and index subtractions are natural numbers; each G value is embedded into the integers before the recurrence arithmetic.\n+\n+**Theorem 1.8 (The recurrence holds from index three).**\n+\n+$$\\exists (N: \\mathbb{N}), ((3 \\le N) \\land (\\forall (n: \\mathbb{N}), ((N \\le n) \\Rightarrow ((\\operatorname{G}\\left(n\\right): \\mathbb{Z}) = 3 \\cdot (\\operatorname{G}\\left(n - 1\\right): \\mathbb{Z}) - 3 \\cdot (\\operatorname{G}\\left(n - 2\\right): \\mathbb{Z}) + (\\operatorname{G}\\left(n - 3\\right): \\mathbb{Z})))))$$\n+\n+*Proof.* Machine-checked in Lean as `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.result` (`✓ std3`). ∎\n+\n+*Resolves.* `Problems/bkm-double-root` (proved) by `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.result`.\n+\n+<!-- scribe-open-problem-resolution-v1 {\"problem_slug\":\"bkm-double-root\",\"declaration_gid\":\"D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.result\",\"resolution_kind\":\"proved\"} -->\n+\n+*Source.* Repository-derived.\n+\n+*Acknowledgement.* Christian Ballot, Clark Kimberling and Peter J. C. Moses (2017). *Linear Recurrences Originating From Polynomial Trees*. DOI: [10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731](https://doi.org/10.1080/00150517.2017.12427731). URL: <https://www.fq.math.ca/Papers1/55-5/BallotKimberlingMoses.pdf>.\n+\n+*Commentary.*\n+\n+Write each reached remainder uniquely as C(a) + C(b) * (X − 1), where a and b are natural numbers. The two children change the coordinates to (a + 1,b) and (a,b + a). After at most n operations the pairs are exactly (0,0), together with 0 < a ≤ n and b ≤ a(n − a). This follows by induction: subtract a from b when b ≥ a, and otherwise decrease a by one. In generation n + 1, the top row consists of (n + 1,0). For each a ≤ n the remaining row is a(n − a) < b ≤ a(n + 1 − a), an interval of exactly a integers. Injectivity of the polynomial labels therefore gives G(n) = 1 + the sum of a over a < n, including the separate zero-root case. Its consecutive differences equal n, so its third finite difference vanishes. Taking N = 3 proves the assertion.\n+\n+## References\n+\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.G`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.addChild`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.claim`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.generation`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.mulChild`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.q`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.result`\n+- Truth anchor: `D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.seen`"},{"sha":"232025c8a9ea00fab09fe40ae68659b0c877eca7","filename":"Blueprint/D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.scribe.cs","status":"added","additions":104,"deletions":0,"changes":104,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/2bd34aa7fd7676d9c4233eeec266df8aa1541d93/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS3%2FCombinatorics%2FPolynomialTrees%2FBallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.scribe.cs","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/2bd34aa7fd7676d9c4233eeec266df8aa1541d93/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS3%2FCombinatorics%2FPolynomialTrees%2FBallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.scribe.cs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/Blueprint%2FD5%2FS3%2FCombinatorics%2FPolynomialTrees%2FBallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.scribe.cs?ref=2bd34aa7fd7676d9c4233eeec266df8aa1541d93","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@\n+using static StrataLint.Scribe.DefinitionDsl;\n+using static StrataLint.Scribe.FormulaDsl;\n+using F = StrataLint.Scribe.FormulaDsl;\n+\n+namespace StrataLint.Scribe.Blueprint.D5.S3.Combinatorics.PolynomialTrees;\n+\n+internal sealed class BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGenerationDocument : IScribeDocumentDefinition\n+{\n+    private const string Module = \"D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration\";\n+    private static readonly LibraryNoteRef Source = LibraryNoteRef.Create(\n+        \"D5/L/RecurrenceComposition/ballotkimberlingmoses2017polynomialtrees\");\n+    private const string OperationsQuote = \"\"\"Section 1, p. 15: “Let T∗ be the set of polynomials in x generated by these rules: 0 ∈ T∗, and if p ∈ T∗, then p + 1 ∈ T∗ and xp ∈ T∗.”\"\"\";\n+    private const string ReductionQuote = \"\"\"Section 1, p. 17: “Then the substitution of qₘ₋₁xᵐ⁻¹ + ⋯ + q₁x + q₀ for xᵐ throughout T∗ produces a labeling of T∗ that includes duplicates.” “For the top-to-bottom order, we denote the resulting tree by T(q(x)).” “Note that T(q(x)) can be regarded as T∗ mod q(x).”\"\"\";\n+    private const string RecurrenceQuote = \"Some proofs of the computer-detected recurrences reported in Table 5 and 6 might be challenging. Most of the entries in the column headed “linear recurrence” are conjectured as “eventual”; i.e., the recurrence applies after some unspecified number of initial terms.\";\n+\n+    public DocumentDefinition Create() => DocumentDefinition.Create(ScribeNode.Create(\n+        \"The polynomial tree modulo X squared minus 2 X plus 1 has generation sizes satisfying the Table 5 recurrence with coefficients 3, -3, 1 at every index at least 3.\",\n+        H(\"The double-root row of Ballot–Kimberling–Moses Table 5\"),\n+        Blocks(\n+            Node(\"q\", \"The double-root polynomial\", Eq(Typed(Q(\"q\"), Polynomials()),\n+                Add(Sub(Pow(Q(\"Polynomial\", \"X\"), D(2)), Mul(D(2), Q(\"Polynomial\", \"X\"))), D(1))),\n+                \"Table 5, p. 23, gives the row q(x) = x² − 2x + 1, Gₙ = 1,1,2,4,7,11,16,22,29,37,46, and linear recurrence 3,−3,1. Here X is Polynomial.X over the integers.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"addChild\", \"The addition child\", All(\"p\", Polynomials(),\n+                Eq(Call(\"addChild\", X(\"p\")), App(Q(\"Polynomial\", \"modByMonic\"), Add(X(\"p\"), D(1)), Q(\"q\")))),\n+                OperationsQuote + \" \" + ReductionQuote + \" The addition child is the monic remainder of p + 1 modulo q in Polynomial ℤ.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"mulChild\", \"The multiplication child\", All(\"p\", Polynomials(),\n+                Eq(Call(\"mulChild\", X(\"p\")), App(Q(\"Polynomial\", \"modByMonic\"), Mul(Q(\"Polynomial\", \"X\"), X(\"p\")), Q(\"q\")))),\n+                OperationsQuote + \" \" + ReductionQuote + \" The multiplication child is the monic remainder of X * p modulo q in Polynomial ℤ.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"seen\", \"All labels reached within a given depth\", And(\n+                Eq(Call(\"seen\", D(0)), SingletonZero()), All(\"n\", Naturals(),\n+                    Eq(Call(\"seen\", Add(X(\"n\"), D(1))), Union(Union(Call(\"seen\", X(\"n\")),\n+                        Image(Q(\"addChild\"), Call(\"seen\", X(\"n\")))), Image(Q(\"mulChild\"), Call(\"seen\", X(\"n\"))))))),\n+                OperationsQuote + \" \" + ReductionQuote + \" The finite set seen n contains every distinct label reached in at most n operations, including the zero root. It accumulates the old labels and both child images, so multiplicities and the choice of a parent among equal labels have no effect.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"generation\", \"The generation sets\", And(\n+                Eq(Call(\"generation\", D(0)), SingletonZero()), All(\"n\", Naturals(),\n+                    Eq(Call(\"generation\", Add(X(\"n\"), D(1))), Seq(Call(\"seen\", Add(X(\"n\"), D(1))), Sp, Setminus, Sp, Call(\"seen\", X(\"n\")))))),\n+                \"\"\"Section 1, p. 15: “We regard T∗ as a tree that grows in successive generations: g(0) = {0}, g(1) = {1}, g(2) = {2,x}, g(3) = {3,2x,x + 1,x²} g(4) = {4,3x,2x + 1,2x²,x + 2,x² + x,x² + 1,x³}, and so on, as in Figure 1.” \"\"\" + ReductionQuote + \" Generation zero is the zero root. At depth n + 1, set difference removes every label seen at an earlier depth. Finset membership counts a same-generation duplicate once. These are polynomial remainders, without evaluating X at 1.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"G\", \"Generation cardinality\", All(\"n\", Naturals(),\n+                Eq(Call(\"G\", X(\"n\")), App(Q(\"Finset\", \"card\"), Call(\"generation\", X(\"n\"))))),\n+                \"\"\"Section 1, p. 17: “Much of the paper henceforth studies the sequence (Gₙ)ₙ≥₀, where Gₙ = |g(n)| and g(n) is the nth generation of the tree T(r), for various r.” Section 5 uses these generation counts for polynomial choices q(x). Here G n is the natural-number cardinality of generation n for the selected polynomial tree.\"\"\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"claim\", \"The eventual recurrence\", Iff(Q(\"claim\"), ClaimBody()),\n+                \"Section 5, p. 23: “\" + RecurrenceQuote + \"” The selected Table 5 row is q(x) = x² − 2x + 1 with recurrence coefficients 3,−3,1. Its assertion is the existence of N ≥ 3 such that the displayed recurrence holds for every n ≥ N. All indices and index subtractions are natural numbers; each G value is embedded into the integers before the recurrence arithmetic.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromLiterature(Source)),\n+            Node(\"result\", \"The recurrence holds from index three\", ClaimBody(),\n+                \"Write each reached remainder uniquely as C(a) + C(b) * (X − 1), where a and b are natural numbers. The two children change the coordinates to (a + 1,b) and (a,b + a). After at most n operations the pairs are exactly (0,0), together with 0 < a ≤ n and b ≤ a(n − a). This follows by induction: subtract a from b when b ≥ a, and otherwise decrease a by one. In generation n + 1, the top row consists of (n + 1,0). For each a ≤ n the remaining row is a(n − a) < b ≤ a(n + 1 − a), an interval of exactly a integers. Injectivity of the polynomial labels therefore gives G(n) = 1 + the sum of a over a < n, including the separate zero-root case. Its consecutive differences equal n, so its third finite difference vanishes. Taking N = 3 proves the assertion.\",\n+                DescribeRole.Theorem, AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(Source),\n+                new OpenProblemResolutionClaim(ProblemSlugRef.Create(\"bkm-double-root\"), ResolutionKind.Proved)))));\n+\n+    private static DocumentBlock Node(string name, string title, Formula formula, string prose,\n+        DescribeRole role, AssessedProvenance provenance, OpenProblemResolutionClaim? resolution = null) => Describe.Lean(\n+            DescribeId.Create(name switch { \"addChild\" => \"add-child\", \"mulChild\" => \"mul-child\", \"G\" => \"cardinality\", _ => name }), DeclarationHandle.Create(Module + \".\" + name), H(title),\n+            StatementSource.FromAuthor(Disp(formula)), provenance, Blocks(Paragraph(Text(prose))), role, resolution);\n+\n+    private static Formula ClaimBody()\n+    {\n+        Formula n = X(\"n\");\n+        Formula rhs = Add(Sub(Mul(D(3), IntegerG(Sub(n, D(1)))),\n+            Mul(D(3), IntegerG(Sub(n, D(2))))), IntegerG(Sub(n, D(3))));\n+        return ExistsOver(\"N\", Naturals(), And(Le(D(3), X(\"N\")), All(\"n\", Naturals(),\n+            Implies(Le(X(\"N\"), n), Eq(IntegerG(n), rhs)))));\n+    }\n+\n+    private static Formula X(string name) => F.Id(name);\n+    private static Formula Naturals() => Seq(Mathbb, Grp(X(\"N\")));\n+    private static Formula Integers() => Seq(Mathbb, Grp(X(\"Z\")));\n+    private static Formula Polynomials() => App(Q(\"Polynomial\"), Integers());\n+    private static Formula IntegerG(Formula n) => Typed(Call(\"G\", n), Integers());\n+    private static Formula SingletonZero() => App(Q(\"Finset\", \"singleton\"), Typed(D(0), Polynomials()));\n+    private static Formula Union(Formula a, Formula b) => App(Q(\"Finset\", \"union\"), a, b);\n+    private static Formula Image(Formula f, Formula a) => App(Q(\"Finset\", \"image\"), f, a);\n+    private static Formula Q(params string[] parts)\n+    {\n+        var items = new System.Collections.Generic.List<Formula>();\n+        foreach (string part in parts)\n+        {\n+            if (items.Count > 0) items.Add(Dot);\n+            items.Add(X(part));\n+        }\n+        return Seq(Operatorname, Grp(Seq([.. items])));\n+    }\n+    private static Formula App(Formula f, params Formula[] args) => new Formula.Apply(f, [.. args]);\n+    private static Formula Call(string name, params Formula[] args) => App(Q(name), args);\n+    private static Formula Parenthesized(Formula x) => Seq(Open, x, Close);\n+    private static Formula Typed(Formula x, Formula type) => Parenthesized(Seq(x, Colon, Sp, type));\n+    private static Formula All(string name, Formula type, Formula body) =>\n+        Seq(Forall, Sp, Typed(X(name), type), Comma, Sp, Parenthesized(body));\n+    private static Formula ExistsOver(string name, Formula type, Formula body) =>\n+        Seq(Exists, Sp, Typed(X(name), type), Comma, Sp, Parenthesized(body));\n+    private static Formula Eq(Formula a, Formula b) => new Formula.Relation(a, FormulaRelationOperator.Equal, b);\n+    private static Formula Le(Formula a, Formula b) => new Formula.Relation(a, FormulaRelationOperator.LessThanOrEqual, b);\n+    private static Formula Add(Formula a, Formula b) => new Formula.Binary(a, FormulaBinaryOperator.Add, b);\n+    private static Formula Sub(Formula a, Formula b) => new Formula.Binary(a, FormulaBinaryOperator.Subtract, b);\n+    private static Formula Mul(Formula a, Formula b) => new Formula.Binary(a, FormulaBinaryOperator.Multiply, b);\n+    private static Formula Pow(Formula a, Formula b) => new Formula.Power(a, b);\n+    private static Formula And(Formula a, Formula b) => new Formula.Logic(Parenthesized(a), FormulaLogicOperator.And, Parenthesized(b));\n+    private static Formula Implies(Formula a, Formula b) => new Formula.Logic(Parenthesized(a), FormulaLogicOperator.Implies, Parenthesized(b));\n+    private static Formula Iff(Formula a, Formula b) => new Formula.Logic(Parenthesized(a), FormulaLogicOperator.Iff, Parenthesized(b));\n+}"},{"sha":"66ab43e61e87ab987e9d2bf065b5a8f3d4a7a16c","filename":"D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.lean","status":"added","additions":373,"deletions":0,"changes":373,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/2bd34aa7fd7676d9c4233eeec266df8aa1541d93/D5%2FS3%2FCombinatorics%2FPolynomialTrees%2FBallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.lean","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/2bd34aa7fd7676d9c4233eeec266df8aa1541d93/D5%2FS3%2FCombinatorics%2FPolynomialTrees%2FBallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.lean","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/D5%2FS3%2FCombinatorics%2FPolynomialTrees%2FBallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.lean?ref=2bd34aa7fd7676d9c4233eeec266df8aa1541d93","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,373 @@\n+/- GID: D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration\n+   generality: I\n+   mirror-B: D5/B/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration\n+   mirror-E: none(waiver:external-open-problem-resolution)\n+   anchors: []\n+   utility: none\n+   digest: Exact double-root tree shells imply the Table 5 recurrence from index three. -/\n+\n+/-\n+proof_shape: result: content; expansion uses seen_spec, an induction carrying exact reach bounds.\n+escape_witness: none; admission uses the external open-problem settlement.\n+admission_basis: open-problem-resolution (#23638; Proved)\n+Direct frozen dependencies: none (pinned Mathlib only).\n+Escape audit unfinished: https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/24117\n+The public definitions retain the polynomial-remainder construction; the private pair model\n+is related to it by seen_spec.\n+Utility none: unbounded exact reachability, shell counting and recurrence; finite root facts\n+are consumed helpers rather than a positive finite-enumeration deliverable.\n+proof_shape: q_square: bind-only; consumers: q_monic, q_degree; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: q_monic: bind-only; consumers: label_mod, mulChild_label; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: q_degree: bind-only; consumers: label_degree; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: label_degree: bind-only; consumers: label_mod; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: label_mod: bind-only; consumers: addChild_label, mulChild_label; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: label_zero: bind-only; consumers: seen_spec; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: label_injective: bind-only; consumers: label_mem_seen, rowLabel_injective, top_not_in_rows; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: addChild_label: bind-only; consumers: seen_spec; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: mulChild_label: bind-only; consumers: seen_spec; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: valid_mono: bind-only; consumers: seen_spec; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: valid_add: bind-only; consumers: seen_spec; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: valid_mul: bind-only; consumers: seen_spec; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: valid_predecessor: bind-only; consumers: seen_spec; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: seen_spec: content; consumers: label_mem_seen, generation_succ_spec; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: label_mem_seen: content; consumers: generation_succ_spec; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: generation_succ_spec: content; consumers: generation_succ_eq; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: rowLabel_injective: bind-only; consumers: G_succ; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: generation_succ_eq: content; consumers: G_succ; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: top_not_in_rows: bind-only; consumers: G_succ; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: G_succ: content; consumers: G_sum; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: G_zero: bind-only; consumers: G_sum; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: G_sum: content; consumers: G_difference; escape_witness: none.\n+proof_shape: G_difference: content; consumers: result; escape_witness: none.\n+-/\n+\n+import Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Div\n+\n+/-! The polynomial-form tree for the double-root row of Table 5.\n+The pair coordinates are proved to describe the literal monic-remainder operations.\n+-/\n+\n+namespace D5.S3.Combinatorics.PolynomialTrees.BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration\n+\n+open Polynomial\n+\n+noncomputable section\n+\n+/-- The fixed polynomial from the selected Table 5 row. -/\n+def q : Polynomial ℤ := X ^ 2 - 2 * X + 1\n+\n+/-- First child, reduced modulo the source's fixed monic polynomial. -/\n+def addChild (p : Polynomial ℤ) : Polynomial ℤ := (p + 1) %ₘ q\n+\n+/-- Second child, reduced modulo the source's fixed monic polynomial. -/\n+def mulChild (p : Polynomial ℤ) : Polynomial ℤ := (X * p) %ₘ q\n+\n+/-- All distinct labels reached by at most n source operations, including the root. -/\n+def seen : ℕ → Finset (Polynomial ℤ)\n+  | 0 => {0}\n+  | n + 1 => seen n ∪ (seen n).image addChild ∪ (seen n).image mulChild\n+\n+/-- Generation zero is the root; later generations delete every earlier label. -/\n+def generation : ℕ → Finset (Polynomial ℤ)\n+  | 0 => {0}\n+  | n + 1 => seen (n + 1) \\ seen n\n+\n+/-- The source's generation-cardinality sequence G_n. -/\n+def G (n : ℕ) : ℕ := (generation n).card\n+\n+/-- The complete eventual-recurrence assertion for the selected Table 5 row. -/\n+def claim : Prop :=\n+  ∃ N : ℕ, 3 ≤ N ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n →\n+    (G n : ℤ) = 3 * (G (n - 1) : ℤ) - 3 * (G (n - 2) : ℤ) + (G (n - 3) : ℤ)\n+\n+end\n+\n+end D5.S3.Combinatorics.PolynomialTrees.BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration\n+\n+set_option maxHeartbeats 200000\n+set_option maxRecDepth 4096\n+\n+namespace D5.S3.Combinatorics.PolynomialTrees.BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration\n+open Polynomial\n+noncomputable section\n+\n+private def label (a b : ℕ) : Polynomial ℤ := C (a : ℤ) + C (b : ℤ) * (X - 1)\n+\n+private theorem q_square : q = (X - C (1 : ℤ)) ^ 2 := by\n+  simpa only [q, map_one, mul_one, one_pow] using (sub_sq (X : Polynomial ℤ) 1).symm\n+\n+private theorem q_monic : q.Monic := by\n+  rw [q_square]\n+  exact (monic_X_sub_C (1 : ℤ)).pow 2\n+\n+private theorem q_degree : q.degree = 2 := by\n+  rw [q_square, degree_pow, degree_X_sub_C]\n+  norm_num\n+\n+private theorem label_degree (a b : ℕ) : (label a b).degree < q.degree := by\n+  rw [q_degree]\n+  apply lt_of_le_of_lt (degree_add_le _ _)\n+  apply max_lt\n+  · exact degree_C_le.trans_lt (by norm_num)\n+  · apply lt_of_le_of_lt (degree_mul_le _ _)\n+    calc\n+      _ ≤ 0 + 1 := add_le_add degree_C_le (by simpa only [map_one] using (degree_X_sub_C (1 : ℤ)).le)\n+      _ < (2 : WithBot ℕ) := by norm_num\n+\n+private theorem label_mod (a b : ℕ) : label a b %ₘ q = label a b := by\n+  exact (modByMonic_eq_self_iff q_monic).mpr (label_degree a b)\n+\n+private theorem label_zero : label 0 0 = 0 := by simp [label]\n+\n+private theorem label_injective : Function.Injective (fun t : ℕ × ℕ => label t.1 t.2) := by\n+  intro ⟨a,b⟩ ⟨c,d⟩ h\n+  have hb : (b : ℤ) = d := by\n+    have hh := congrArg (fun p : Polynomial ℤ => p.coeff 1) h\n+    simpa [label, coeff_add, coeff_C_mul, coeff_sub, coeff_one, coeff_X] using hh\n+  have ha : (a : ℤ) = c := by\n+    have hh := congrArg (fun p : Polynomial ℤ => p.eval 1) h\n+    simpa [label] using hh\n+  exact Prod.ext (by exact_mod_cast ha) (by exact_mod_cast hb)\n+\n+private theorem addChild_label (a b : ℕ) : addChild (label a b) = label (a+1) b := by\n+  unfold addChild\n+  have h : label a b + 1 = label (a+1) b := by simp [label, Nat.cast_add, map_add]; ring\n+  rw [h, label_mod]\n+\n+private theorem mulChild_label (a b : ℕ) : mulChild (label a b) = label a (b+a) := by\n+  unfold mulChild\n+  calc\n+    (X * label a b) %ₘ q = label a (b+a) %ₘ q := by\n+      apply modByMonic_eq_of_dvd_sub q_monic\n+      refine ⟨C (b : ℤ), ?_⟩\n+      simp [label, q, Nat.cast_add, map_add]\n+      ring\n+    _ = _ := label_mod _ _\n+\n+\n+\n+private def valid (n a b : ℕ) : Prop :=\n+  (a = 0 ∧ b = 0) ∨ (0 < a ∧ a ≤ n ∧ b ≤ a * (n-a))\n+\n+private theorem valid_mono {n a b : ℕ} (h : valid n a b) : valid (n+1) a b := by\n+  rcases h with h | ⟨ha,han,hb⟩\n+  · exact Or.inl h\n+  · exact Or.inr ⟨ha, by omega, hb.trans (Nat.mul_le_mul_left a (by omega))⟩\n+\n+private theorem valid_add {n a b : ℕ} (h : valid n a b) : valid (n+1) (a+1) b := by\n+  rcases h with ⟨rfl,rfl⟩ | ⟨ha,han,hb⟩\n+  · exact Or.inr ⟨by omega,by omega,by omega⟩\n+  · apply Or.inr\n+    refine ⟨by omega,by omega,?_⟩\n+    have he : n+1-(a+1) = n-a := by exact Nat.add_sub_add_right n 1 a\n+    rw [he]\n+    nlinarith\n+\n+private theorem valid_mul {n a b : ℕ} (h : valid n a b) : valid (n+1) a (b+a) := by\n+  rcases h with ⟨rfl,rfl⟩ | ⟨ha,han,hb⟩\n+  · exact Or.inl ⟨rfl,rfl⟩\n+  · apply Or.inr\n+    refine ⟨ha,by omega,?_⟩\n+    have he : n+1-a = n-a+1 := by exact Nat.sub_add_comm han\n+    rw [he]\n+    nlinarith\n+\n+private theorem valid_predecessor {n a b : ℕ} (ha : 0 < a) (han : a ≤ n+1)\n+    (hb : b ≤ a * (n+1-a)) :\n+    (∃ c, valid n c b ∧ c+1=a) ∨\n+    (∃ d, valid n a d ∧ d+a=b) := by\n+  by_cases hab : a ≤ b\n+  · right\n+    have han' : a ≤ n := by\n+      by_contra h\n+      have he : n+1-a=0 := by omega\n+      rw [he, Nat.mul_zero] at hb\n+      omega\n+    refine ⟨b-a, Or.inr ⟨ha,han',?_⟩,by omega⟩\n+    have he : n+1-a=n-a+1 := by exact Nat.sub_add_comm han'\n+    rw [he] at hb\n+    have hh : b-a+a=b := by exact Nat.sub_add_cancel hab\n+    nlinarith\n+  · left\n+    refine ⟨a-1,?_,by omega⟩\n+    by_cases ha1 : a=1\n+    · subst a\n+      have hb0 : b=0 := by exact Nat.eq_zero_of_not_pos hab\n+      simp [valid,hb0]\n+    · apply Or.inr\n+      refine ⟨by omega,by omega,?_⟩\n+      by_cases han' : a ≤ n\n+      · have ht : 1 ≤ n-(a-1) := by omega\n+        have hm := Nat.mul_le_mul_left (a-1) ht\n+        simp only [Nat.mul_one] at hm\n+        omega\n+      · have he : n+1-a=0 := by omega\n+        rw [he, Nat.mul_zero] at hb\n+        omega\n+\n+private theorem seen_spec (n : ℕ) (p : Polynomial ℤ) :\n+    p ∈ seen n ↔ ∃ a b, p = label a b ∧ valid n a b := by\n+  classical\n+  induction n generalizing p with\n+  | zero =>\n+    simp only [seen, Finset.mem_singleton]\n+    constructor\n+    · rintro rfl\n+      exact ⟨0,0,label_zero.symm,Or.inl ⟨rfl,rfl⟩⟩\n+    · rintro ⟨a,b,rfl,h⟩\n+      rcases h with ⟨rfl,rfl⟩ | ⟨ha,han,hb⟩\n+      · exact label_zero\n+      · omega\n+  | succ n ih =>\n+    simp only [seen, Finset.mem_union, Finset.mem_image]\n+    constructor\n+    · rintro ((hp | ⟨r,hr,rfl⟩) | ⟨r,hr,rfl⟩)\n+      · obtain ⟨a,b,rfl,hv⟩ := (ih p).mp hp\n+        exact ⟨a,b,rfl,valid_mono hv⟩\n+      · obtain ⟨a,b,rfl,hv⟩ := (ih r).mp hr\n+        exact ⟨a+1,b,addChild_label a b,valid_add hv⟩\n+      · obtain ⟨a,b,rfl,hv⟩ := (ih r).mp hr\n+        exact ⟨a,b+a,mulChild_label a b,valid_mul hv⟩\n+    · rintro ⟨a,b,rfl,hv⟩\n+      rcases hv with ⟨rfl,rfl⟩ | ⟨ha,han,hb⟩\n+      · exact Or.inl (Or.inl ((ih _).mpr ⟨0,0,rfl,Or.inl ⟨rfl,rfl⟩⟩))\n+      · rcases valid_predecessor ha han hb with ⟨c,hc,hca⟩ | ⟨d,hd,hdb⟩\n+        · left; right\n+          exact ⟨label c b,(ih _).mpr ⟨c,b,rfl,hc⟩,by rw [addChild_label,hca]⟩\n+        · right\n+          exact ⟨label a d,(ih _).mpr ⟨a,d,rfl,hd⟩,by rw [mulChild_label,hdb]⟩\n+\n+private theorem label_mem_seen (n a b : ℕ) : label a b ∈ seen n ↔ valid n a b := by\n+  rw [seen_spec]\n+  constructor\n+  · rintro ⟨c,d,h,hv⟩\n+    have hh := label_injective (show label (a,b).1 (a,b).2 = label (c,d).1 (c,d).2 from h)\n+    cases hh\n+    exact hv\n+  · intro h\n+    exact ⟨a,b,rfl,h⟩\n+\n+\n+private theorem generation_succ_spec (n : ℕ) (p : Polynomial ℤ) :\n+    p ∈ generation (n+1) ↔ p = label (n+1) 0 ∨\n+      ∃ a b, a ≤ n ∧ a*(n-a) < b ∧ b ≤ a*(n+1-a) ∧ p = label a b := by\n+  classical\n+  simp only [generation, Finset.mem_sdiff]\n+  constructor\n+  · rintro ⟨hp,hn⟩\n+    obtain ⟨a,b,rfl,hv⟩ := (seen_spec (n+1) p).mp hp\n+    rw [label_mem_seen] at hn\n+    rcases hv with ⟨rfl,rfl⟩ | ⟨ha,han,hb⟩\n+    · exact False.elim (hn (Or.inl ⟨rfl,rfl⟩))\n+    · by_cases htop : a=n+1\n+      · subst a\n+        have hb0 : b=0 := by simpa using hb\n+        subst b\n+        exact Or.inl rfl\n+      · right\n+        have han' : a ≤ n := by omega\n+        refine ⟨a,b,han',?_,hb,rfl⟩\n+        by_contra hh\n+        exact hn (Or.inr ⟨ha,han',by omega⟩)\n+  · rintro (rfl | ⟨a,b,han,hlo,hhi,rfl⟩)\n+    · rw [label_mem_seen,label_mem_seen]\n+      constructor\n+      · exact Or.inr ⟨by omega,by omega,by simp⟩\n+      · intro h\n+        rcases h with ⟨ha,hb⟩ | ⟨ha,han,hb⟩ <;> omega\n+    · rw [label_mem_seen,label_mem_seen]\n+      have ha : 0<a := by\n+        by_contra h\n+        have he : a=0 := by exact Nat.eq_zero_of_not_pos h\n+        simp [he] at hhi\n+        omega\n+      constructor\n+      · exact Or.inr ⟨ha,by omega,hhi⟩\n+      · intro h\n+        rcases h with ⟨he,hb⟩ | ⟨ha,han,hb⟩\n+        · omega\n+        · omega\n+\n+private def shellRows (n : ℕ) : Finset (Σ _ : ℕ, ℕ) :=\n+  (Finset.range (n+1)).sigma (fun a => Finset.Ioc (a*(n-a)) (a*(n+1-a)))\n+\n+\n+private theorem rowLabel_injective : Function.Injective (fun t : Σ _ : ℕ, ℕ => label t.1 t.2) := by\n+  intro ⟨a,b⟩ ⟨c,d⟩ h\n+  have hh := label_injective (show label (a,b).1 (a,b).2 = label (c,d).1 (c,d).2 from h)\n+  cases hh\n+  rfl\n+\n+private theorem generation_succ_eq (n : ℕ) : generation (n+1) =\n+    insert (label (n+1) 0) ((shellRows n).image (fun t : Σ _ : ℕ, ℕ => label t.1 t.2)) := by\n+  classical\n+  ext p\n+  rw [generation_succ_spec]\n+  simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_image, shellRows, Finset.mem_sigma,\n+    Finset.mem_range, Finset.mem_Ioc, Sigma.exists]\n+  constructor\n+  · rintro (h | ⟨a,b,ha,hlo,hhi,hp⟩)\n+    · exact Or.inl h\n+    · exact Or.inr ⟨a,b,⟨by omega,hlo,hhi⟩,hp.symm⟩\n+  · rintro (h | ⟨a,b,⟨ha,hlo,hhi⟩,hp⟩)\n+    · exact Or.inl h\n+    · exact Or.inr ⟨a,b,by omega,hlo,hhi,hp.symm⟩\n+\n+private theorem top_not_in_rows (n : ℕ) : label (n+1) 0 ∉ (shellRows n).image (fun t : Σ _ : ℕ, ℕ => label t.1 t.2) := by\n+  classical\n+  rintro h\n+  obtain ⟨⟨a,b⟩,hm,he⟩ := Finset.mem_image.mp h\n+  have hh := label_injective (show label (a,b).1 (a,b).2 = label (n+1,0).1 (n+1,0).2 from he)\n+  have ha : a=n+1 := congrArg Prod.fst hh\n+  have hr : a<n+1 := Finset.mem_range.mp (Finset.mem_sigma.mp hm).1\n+  omega\n+\n+private theorem G_succ (n : ℕ) : G (n+1) = 1 + ∑ a ∈ Finset.range (n+1), a := by\n+  classical\n+  unfold G\n+  rw [generation_succ_eq, Finset.card_insert_of_notMem (top_not_in_rows n),\n+    Finset.card_image_of_injective _ rowLabel_injective]\n+  unfold shellRows\n+  rw [Finset.card_sigma]\n+  have he : ∀ a ∈ Finset.range (n+1),\n+      (Finset.Ioc (a*(n-a)) (a*(n+1-a))).card = a := by\n+    intro a ha\n+    have han : a≤n := by exact Finset.mem_range_succ_iff.mp ha\n+    have hs : n+1-a=n-a+1 := by exact Nat.sub_add_comm han\n+    rw [Nat.card_Ioc,hs,Nat.mul_add,Nat.mul_one,Nat.add_sub_cancel_left]\n+  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl he]\n+  omega\n+\n+private theorem G_zero : G 0 = 1 := by\n+  exact Finset.card_singleton (0 : Polynomial ℤ)\n+\n+private theorem G_sum (n : ℕ) : G n = 1 + ∑ a ∈ Finset.range n, a := by\n+  cases n with\n+  | zero => simp [G_zero]\n+  | succ n => exact G_succ n\n+\n+private theorem G_difference (n : ℕ) : G (n+1) = G n + n := by\n+  rw [G_sum,G_sum,Finset.sum_range_succ]\n+  omega\n+\n+theorem result : claim := by\n+  refine ⟨3,by omega,?_⟩\n+  intro n hn\n+  have h1 := G_difference (n-1)\n+  have h2 := G_difference (n-2)\n+  have h3 := G_difference (n-3)\n+  have e1 : n-1+1=n := by omega\n+  have e2 : n-2+1=n-1 := by omega\n+  have e3 : n-3+1=n-2 := by omega\n+  rw [e1] at h1\n+  rw [e2] at h2\n+  rw [e3] at h3\n+  have h1z : (G n : ℤ) = (G (n-1) : ℤ) + (n-1 : ℕ) := by exact congrArg Nat.cast h1\n+  have h2z : (G (n-1) : ℤ) = (G (n-2) : ℤ) + (n-2 : ℕ) := by exact congrArg Nat.cast h2\n+  have h3z : (G (n-2) : ℤ) = (G (n-3) : ℤ) + (n-3 : ℕ) := by exact congrArg Nat.cast h3\n+  have hh : ((n-1 : ℕ) : ℤ) - 2*((n-2 : ℕ) : ℤ) + ((n-3 : ℕ) : ℤ) = 0 := by omega\n+  omega\n+\n+\n+end\n+end D5.S3.Combinatorics.PolynomialTrees.BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration"},{"sha":"5c69dc1b3a1801e9a86651b05b6afd5c70947c7a","filename":"Golden/Frozen/state/D5/S3/Combinatorics/PolynomialTrees/BallotKimberlingMosesDoubleRootGeneration.lean.json","statu